// ── the clock ───────────────────────────────────────────
// PHASE timing and TRANSITION timing are separate systems.
//
// A phase has a DURATION: how long until the next phase
// begins. That is all. It says nothing about how long the
// moves inside it take, and it is not derived from them.
//
// The previous clock computed each phase start FROM the move
// length (setS = rackE + gap), which made overlap structurally
// impossible — a phase could never begin until the one before
// it had finished moving. Now the phases are a plain
// accumulation of their own durations, so setting T Settle
// shorter than a settle move (3 * Hold Frames) starts the fill
// while the seed and handoff are still travelling.
